# Protect committed binary artifacts from line-ending conversion.
#
# This is not cosmetic. data/processed/subsample.parquet and cache/llm_cache.sqlite
# are committed so the pipeline reproduces without a Kaggle account or an API key
# (decision_log.md D10). If git ever applied CRLF conversion to them, the file on
# a fresh clone would differ byte-for-byte from the one here and
# tests/test_subsample.py's byte-identity check would fail on someone else's
# machine -- exactly where it matters most.
*.parquet   binary
*.sqlite    binary
*.png       binary
*.pkl       binary
*.npy       binary

# Normalise text so the repo is stable across platforms.
*.py        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.jsonl     text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
*.in        text eol=lf
